{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system","id":1079494,"title":"Lunars and interacting with the base Crafting system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-16T13:38:56-07:00","id":1079494,"title":"Lunars and interacting with the base Crafting system","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1078906-lunar-exclusive-infrastructure?p=1078966#post1078966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars biggest problem isn't what infrastructure that they have, it's whether or not they'll have Charms that will make it easier to handle things related to crafting slots, coloured experience, and the terminus to extended crafting rolls.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't really think they should. Maybe a few things to craft a bit better than a mortal would, but particularly not things that overturn assumptions about how many magical things have been made in the Second Age. Thus, it's not a matter of Lunars being unable to make anything, just the natural assumption that they've not made much if they have to follow the base Artifact and Wonder crafting rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bPartially because I don't think it's something as natural to them when they don't have Charms extending out of the Craft Ability, and partially because it's not something I see being a particular forte of their characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this fly in the face of Holden's words that Lunar Exalted are capable of making amazing things in caves with boxes of scraps?<br /> <br /> Why <i>shouldn't </i>Lunar Charms grant them project slots, colored experience, or extended termini? Should they likewise be incapable of enhancing War-based strategem rolls because they don't have War Charms? Are these not both mental tasks that Intelligence Charms could cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:59:10-07:00","id":1079502,"title":"","content":"To me it seems necessary for them to have at least <i>some</i> interaction with the craft system simply because having to farming enough gold crafting xp to start work on a Moonsilver daiklave, failing to hit enough successes and having to start from scratch in the knowledge that you cannot do better next time - does not seem like my idea of a good time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:04:10-07:00","id":1079507,"title":"","content":"I suspect the only deficiency Lunars will have in the second age is the generation of White Experience, and expect them to be quite good in all other areas. Of COURSE your New Moon smith can produce daiklaves and wonders easily, just not the wonders of the First Age or works of singular artifice.<br /> <br /> Even then, Lunars in the Second age have created a new goddamn Loom of Fate that covers a region as large as France.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:40:14-07:00","id":1079579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system#post1079494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't this fly in the face of Holden's words that Lunar Exalted are capable of making amazing things in caves with boxes of scraps?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Does</i> it?<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, just going with the base rules, <i>occasionally</i> producing wonders can be done with some combination of time, the right ingredients, and high dice pools, no fistful of Craft Charms or unique infrastructure required.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople have done the math on this, after all. The largest single obstacle to <i>mortals</i> making Artifacts is that it's just not an action they're permitted by the rules to take. (The second and third obstacles being the limited Terminus and the high difficulty, respectively.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-16-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:54:23-07:00","id":1079617,"title":"","content":"I assume Lunars will have some charms related to Crafting, but they will be filtered through their particular themes. It's not going to be so straight forward as adding more slots, dice, etc. This is a natural side effect of moving away from Lunars having I Can't Believe They Aren't Solar Charms(tm).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:08:35-07:00","id":1079626,"title":"","content":"Judging by how unhappy a lot of people are with the Crafting system, the idea that Lunars don't get to deal with it could be viewed as a plus. (Note: that's a joke). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, I can understand where Isator is coming from. The Second Age is written under the assumption that Lunar Elders aren't pumping out 5 dot or N/A artifacts with any kind of regularity, which is what you would generally expect an Elder craftsman could do. Especially if elder Lunars don't need vast infrastructure to make those kind of artifacts - the natural question arises, why don't they make them? And if they can make them with some regularity, then you're left wondering why Lunars and their servants aren't often decked out with those kind of powerful artifacts. <br /> <br /> But I feel that simply saying, &quot;Sorry but Lunars are the Exalted who can't craft stuff,&quot; also isn't a very good direction to go. <br /> <br /> I would hope that Vance and Minton can hammer out a middle ground between the two extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:11:37-07:00","id":1079627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system#post1079494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't this fly in the face of Holden's words that Lunar Exalted are capable of making amazing things in caves with boxes of scraps?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHe said those were things like veils and amulets.<br /> <br /> So, probably two-dot Artifacts.<br /> <br /> \u200bBy my standards, producing those things with anything less than a nicely stocked, dedicated workshop is quite an achievement. For the moment, I don't think even Solars can do it.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut Solars with the appropriate tools can put a lot of dice and successes into their crafting projects, as well as extend the terminus and even cover some of the experience costs. So creating the highest level Artifacts is a lot more feasible to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's the thing, isn't it? The crafting system would have to grapple with the problem of how to make creation of Artifacts adhere to the presentation of the Age of Sorrows while not falling back on the old problems of being entirely locked behind age requirements or a single cap-breaking Charm for Solars, and all but forbidden to everybody else, and arrived at a solution of a base system in which the requirements to make more powerful Artifacts are standardised across the board as, well, virtually impossible.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo how good that, say, the Dragon Blooded are depends on what assets they have to make it less impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why <i>shouldn't </i>Lunar Charms grant them project slots, colored experience, or extended termini?</div> </div> </div> </div>To my mind, it starts with needing to not make the Lunars look as though they could have engaged in the same kind of crafting that Solars could have, but just failed to for unspecified reasons.<br /> <br /> Again.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and how I personally wouldn't see Craft as being a big thing for Lunars. Not as a case of no Lunars crafting, but rather that I wouldn't picture there as being a Lunar dedicated to it in the same way a Solar artisan or engineer would be.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would approach more from the direction of what ways a Lunar can utilise crafting to the characteristics of being a Lunar in general and their Caste in specific, and the social context that they occupy, rather than how they can use being a Lunar to come up with being the best crafter that they can be.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and I speculate on how some of those goals could be accomplished mechanically, and it does seem to come back to the old problem of doing something the way Solars would, just not as good. I think more satisfaction might be gotten out of Lunars by having them go in a different direction, and I think that the use of Attributes accomplishes that nicely. I've actually thought for a while that an advantage of Attribute Charms is being able to build a given group without having to give equal emphasis to all of the Abilities, which I think might be the best approach for Lunars if something like the eclectic weirdness of Sidereals is off the table.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should they likewise be incapable of enhancing War-based strategem rolls because they don't have War Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can probably enhance rolls with their Excellency, and maybe some other Charms. If it's a question of whether there's a dedicated Lunar general to be extrapolated from their Charm cascade... I actually don't think that should be the case.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like the example I've frequently gone back to with a Lunar sailor, in that I don't really see there as being one. I see Lunars who would be good on boats, some of whom can even do so despite not actually having any Sail (and depending on their Attributes and whether they can double dip their Excellency, might still roll as well as seasoned nautical coves), but that there isn't a sailor archetype that translates directly into Lunars. Among the alternatives is the fact that the Lunar gets to drop into the water and turn into a kraken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these not both mental tasks that Intelligence Charms could cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat depends on what the purpose of Attribute Charms is; are they about being generally good at applying the Attribute in a manner similar to Solars with Abilities, or is it about wielding the Attribute in a manner demonstrative of the Lunar type.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't see the Lunar Intelligence as it relates to Craft being a matter of being generally good at crafting because they're smart; I see it as including, but not limited to, the Lunar being very smart about things like how to break the possessions of enemies and prey. Or how to build things on a tight budget that can efficiently break the enemies or prey (while still actually being triggered like things on a tight budget; when you put a lot of nails and glass with kerosene into a container with a cordite trigger, you're going to get something that fills the enemy with nails and glass, and not a nuclear bomb).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:56:04-07:00","id":1079644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1077196#post1077196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars aren't &quot;supposed&quot; to be bad at crafting, bureaucracy, or calligraphy. There aren't things they definitely absolutely don't do. They have a distinct thematic foundation and conceptual paradigm for their power, which guides the ways in which they realize certain powers, but doesn't forbid things outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for why elder Lunars don't just keep cranking out artifacts, not every elder Lunar is a crafter, and there comes a point when the Silver Pact has enough Artifacts to keep up with and making any more would just be risking letting some fall into enemy hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:39:57-07:00","id":1079661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079644#post1079644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for why elder Lunars don't just keep cranking out artifacts, not every elder Lunar is a crafter, and there comes a point when the Silver Pact has enough Artifacts to keep up with and making any more would just be risking letting some fall into enemy hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reiterating: Yes, they're actually holding territory against the Dragon-Blooded this time instead of being pushed to the farthest reaches of Creation, but NPCs don't work like PCs. Ma Ha Suchi doesn't get to go &quot;Hmm yes my ability to murder Dragon-Blooded is adequately developed, I'm going to start dumping my XP into crafting and become the best Lunar Craftsman there is.&quot;; he has the charms he needs to fulfill his goals and drives; the age of &quot;Any NPC of this age would have so much EXP they just have Everything in the charmset&quot; is supposed to be pretty well over. So &quot;If Lunars can be good Crafters then we must assume there are workshops of 50+ Lunars pumping out 3-5 dot daiklaves with extreme frequency, which disrupts the setting, therefore Lunars must not have even a single non-excellency Crafting charm&quot; works from faulty logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:00:35-07:00","id":1079670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system#post1079494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't this fly in the face of Holden's words that Lunar Exalted are capable of making amazing things in caves with boxes of scraps?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Capable of&quot; is different from &quot;can do easily.&quot; Like I said in the other thread - just because Tony Stark can make something amazing in a cave with a box of scraps doesn't mean he does his best work there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079627#post1079627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He said those were things like veils and amulets.<br /> <br /> So, probably two-dot Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go that far. For one thing, it's boring! You do want to be able to tell stories of artifacts, like Tony Stark's armor, that were made in difficult and unlikely situations.<br /> <br /> However, the key here is difficult and unlikely. Tony Stark making his armor in a cave from a box of scraps is legendary because it is <i>hard</i>, even for him - in a comic or movie we sort of gloss over what that means, but he was driven by a mortal injury, and we can assume he wouldn't be able to do it under lesser circumstances.<br /> <br /> Doing it in Exalted works the same way. I think they can make more than two-dot stuff in a cave - but even more than usual, making really world-shaking stuff under those conditions takes great time, and effort, and personal investment, and perhaps a degree of risk, whether it's risking failures, or taking more mundane risks to raid and seize arcane ingredients that they need, attracting attention to themselves; or cutting deals with spirits and so on.<br /> <br /> (Of course, you could argue that when you're cutting deals with spirits and stealing supplies from caravans, beyond a certain point your cave isn't so much a cave as it is the heart of a huge web of schemes to get you the stuff you'd normally have in a well-equipped lab - but it's doable, at least. WST aside, you can't just make a four or five-dot artifact from nothingness, but it's perfectly plausible that an obsessive enough Lunar with enough time to brood over it could get their hands on what they need.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system#post1079494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why <i>shouldn't </i>Lunar Charms grant them project slots, colored experience, or extended termini? Should they likewise be incapable of enhancing War-based strategem rolls because they don't have War Charms? Are these not both mental tasks that Intelligence Charms could cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, again, there's a huge amount of space between &quot;capable of&quot; and &quot;gets all the tools Solars get.&quot; Read Vance's post more carefully. Lunars do have an approach to crafting, but Vance is careful to word it lightly (it's something that &quot;isn't forbidden outright&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Whereas, say, for Solars or Alchemicals (or most Ability-based Exalted), crafting is <i>central</i>. It gets entire charm trees and massive focus. Lunar crafting is more like, say... Solar teleportation or illusions or summoning hard-light constructs. These are things that their charmset does (even if it sometimes avoids the exact words), when it's appropriate; but it's not something presented as core to being a Solar or as something a typical Solar would specialize in, and there's no one charm tree you'd go into to be a Solar Master of those things. Whereas, say, an Infernal might have a dedicated charm-tree for each, making it easy to play an Infernal who has mastery in one of those areas as their &quot;thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> To be more specific, the way I see Lunar crafting working is in a bunch of charms scattered over their charmsets that help you craft often-incidentally (plus perhaps a few more directly craft-focused upgrades to these.) For example - you might have the ability to turn hairs from your tail or head into duplicates to help you with tasks; or you might have an Intelligence charm that lets you make a general plan to help you with something complex; or a Strength charm that lets you both sunder things and change their shape; and these will <i>also</i> help you craft (possibly with rules for interacting with the crafting system), and may have upgrades that do nothing but help you craft.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't be surprised if Lunars lacked a single, dedicated, one-stop crafting charm tree like the one used by most Ability-based Exalted. Thematically, this would move away from the idea that &quot;crafter&quot; is a core Lunar concept - it's still available as eg. something your &quot;clever Lunar&quot; or &quot;tricksy Lunar&quot; <i>does</i> with their cleverness or tricksiness, but it isn't a &quot;default&quot; build the way eg. Melee Dawn or Craft Twilight is; it is just one small facet of your New Moon's cleverness, whereas you can easily make a Twilight for whom crafting is their whole thing.<br /> <br /> I think this is what Vance meant when he mentioned a &quot;distinct thematic foundation and conceptual paradigm for their power, which guides the ways in which they realize certain powers&quot; (since it was presented as a &quot;but&quot; to the fact that they do have crafting powers.) Crafting is something they do, but it's something they do on the leaves and edges of their charm tree rather than being a central branch, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:24:38-07:00","id":1079678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079670#post1079670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, again, there's a huge amount of space between &quot;capable of&quot; and &quot;gets all the tools Solars get.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Solars have a <i>lot</i> of tools related to project slots, crafting experience, and terminus-extension.<br /> <br /> There's a huge difference between Lunars getting a few Charms of that sort, and them getting NO Charms of that sort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I wouldn't be surprised if Lunars lacked a single, dedicated, one-stop crafting charm tree like the one used by most Ability-based Exalted. </div> </div> </div>They've NEVER had one. Not even in First Edition's incestuous Lunar Charm trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T22:21:35-07:00","id":1079682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079678#post1079678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've NEVER had one. Not even in First Edition's incestuous Lunar Charm trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but Lunars have not-had a lot of things, and no version of their charmset has ever been ideal. I wouldn't expect them to have it even in 3e, though; and I think that that covers a lot of what people are discussing above (ie. Lunars are capable of crafting, but aren't really craft-focused.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T23:27:11-07:00","id":1079694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079682#post1079682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, but Lunars have not-had a lot of things, and no version of their charmset has ever been ideal. I wouldn't expect them to have it even in 3e, though; and I think that that covers a lot of what people are discussing above (ie. Lunars are capable of crafting, but aren't really craft-focused.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies; I think I was not clear.<br /> <br /> I didn't understand why anyone would complain about the Lunar Exalted lacking a singular Crafting-related Charm tree. I've never seen anyone argue that they should have one, and they have never had one before, so it seemed like an odd point to bring up at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case &quot;Project slots are an abstract representation of how well the character can split focus between multiple significant projects at once.&quot; Splitting focus is definitely something Lunar Exalted can be good at, though of course a Solar craftsman should be much better at applying this to crafting.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know how Lunar Charms should be able to approach Artifact crafting, or even Superior Projects.<br /> <br /> What might be neat are Charms which reward Lunar Exalted with more crafting experience for the (relatively) fewer projects he DOES undertake and complete. All of the criteria for earning crafting experience seem important to Lunars -- wooing people, helping people they love, and solving practical problems. This would, in turn, allow Lunars to get by with crafting far less, while stocking up points to spend on the few serious projects they attempt.<br /> <br /> <br /> What might also be neat is a Charm that permanently gives a Lunar a FOURTH criteria for earning crafting experience: Fashioning a trophy or functional tool out of the corpse of something whose Heart's Blood the Lunar took. It might also work when fashioning such a thing for another Lunar, if they were the one to take the kill and Heart's Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:00:16-07:00","id":1079737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079670#post1079670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go that far. For one thing, it's boring! You do want to be able to tell stories of artifacts, like Tony Stark's armor, that were made in difficult and unlikely situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSpeaking as a person who recently got through a tirade of calling the depiction of the akuma in prior Editions boring, I feel as though &quot;that's boring&quot; has become another one of those overused generic criticisms that has kind of stopped meaning anything, like when people call basically every character beat that they personally dislike &quot;deprotagonizing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm sure there's a fallacy describing the act with engaging with an argument by its terminology rather than its substance, so...<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, I don't really want to tell stories of Artifacts like that. No, that's not right... I don't want it to be standardised and codified in the way it would be with a Charm. As I said elsewhere, the in-character resources needed for any given project are already abstract, so for narratives relating to exceptional circumstances where a character, even a Solar, creates a sister for Volcano Cutter in a much less sophisticated environment than that inverted volcano manse, I would be inclined to bring that more out of setup in the game, with stunts, a sequence of roleplaying events, and a bit of fast-talking the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> It's not as if Solars don't already have a lot of Charms to boost the actual mechanical side of it, so it's nowhere near a case of just reducing the thing to the dreaded Storyteller fiat, it's just one particular aspect in which I think presenting it as extraordinary is something that I think should be hovering outside of mechanical resolutions.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen it comes to Lunars, my current inclination is towards the idea that pulling off whatever caper is required to make the most powerful Artifacts despite most of the infrastructure being in the hands of the enemy is something that has been done, it's not <b>a</b> thing that <u>Lunars</u> do. It's a character's story, rather than a detail of the archetype from which the Lunar gameplay emerges.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not trying to guess at what John or Holden or Vance or Eric have in mind, just expressing my own preferences combined with my lines of inspiration that come out of a statement like that.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso trying to feel out the limits that the crafting system might present to different characters. It's like Alveua; she's a Second Circle Demon with a crafting focus who has been given a fairly decent Charm that can efficiently produce two-dots, reasonably pull off three, and on occasions where she's very lucky get four, so I would shape some of my expectations on what you ask her to make out of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's also the matter of, having established that the infrastructure is important, one is a bit limited in how much can be given to characters without it. Maybe there could be compromises in which one writes a Charm with a lot of caveats and conditions for how it can be used, but I think that makes for unattractive Charms in general, I wouldn't find it to fit with my understanding of what even Lunar Charms are, and it feels like putting the cart before the horse.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, I'd also have a sense of a Charm to reduce the time required before making the first roll of a low-level Artifact to be <i>really</i> quick, quicker than the Solar Charm, offset by not having anything like the rest of the crafting suite.<br /> <br /> \u200bReally, my initial examples of things like slots and coloured exp may not even be the best support of my own idea, since some kind of manipulation of those feels like it could go along with an image of Lunars who get out things that are quick and cheap for circumstantial benefits. The specifics did not matter back there, I was just trying to focus on what is in the actual Crafting system, and what Solars get to manipulate it, to find key points to contest for other crafters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:59:27-07:00","id":1079872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079670#post1079670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is what Vance meant when he mentioned a &quot;distinct thematic foundation and conceptual paradigm for their power, which guides the ways in which they realize certain powers&quot; (since it was presented as a &quot;but&quot; to the fact that they do have crafting powers.) Crafting is something they do, but it's something they do on the leaves and edges of their charm tree rather than being a central branch, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this tree thinking is quite a fruitful (groan) way of thinking about it; what are the actual tree structures we're thinking about for &quot;Craft Charms&quot; for Lunars?<br /> <br /> A couple of extremes along here are:<br /> <br /> 1) An approach where you have what is essentially a Craft tree embedded within a single Attribute. So your Lunar pumps her Intelligence, or whatnot, to meet whatever the maximum requirements for her Craft Charms, and then you just buy linearly up for her through increasing Craft Charms that are all in that Attribute.<br /> <br /> Pros: This actually allows players with an interest to play a Craft specialised Attribute Exalted.<br /> <br /> Cons: Seems is a little dull, in that it's just emulating the Ability based set up, and gives not much flavour of being an Attribute based as opposed to Ability based Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2) The approach which I think Aquillion describes, where Craft Charms are all leaves in the Lunar forest. You'll stumble across them as you journey through the forest, and eventually you'll accumulate a nice enough set of them to put something serious and nice together, but you couldn't systematically build up quickly to be very good at crafting very well or quickly.<br /> <br /> Pros: Really far away from being Ability based.<br /> <br /> Cons: Really quite a frustrating design if your goal is for your character to be good at anything covered by an Ability niche, like Craft, and to fit into a mixed Circle with Ability Exalts as a specialist.<br /> <br /> There are a *lot* of middle structures between thesee.<br /> <br /> One that seems naively quite appealing to me would be as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Lots of fairly low prereq Craft boosters across a bunch of different Attributes - Strength, Stamina, Dex, Perception, etc. Represent applying the Attribute, shapeshifting power and animal qualities to Craft (speed, strength, precision, tirelessness, keen senses, etc). These are easy to buy into for a character who *hasn't* really specialized into that Attribute at all, and who doesn't have that Attribute as favoured. They're also easy entry, so you don't have to buy through a lot of unrelated Charms around combat, environmental perception etc. to get to them.<br /> <br /> 2. However, a large bulk of Craft stuff is also within one of two mental attributes. Probably Wits (quick or intuitive crafting) and Intelligence (slower, planned, deliberate, reasoned). These mostly build on one another. So it is possible to invest in a few places and build up a Craft specialist.<br /> <br /> So I think that strikes a nice balance between avoiding the downsides of a set up where you just have a Craft subtree within an Attribute, and you're virtually Silver Solaring it, while also avoiding the pitfalls of a Charmcloud, where everything you want to play a specific archetype or specialist is so randomly strewn that there's an element of forced multiclassing and playing a specialist isn't so possible.<br /> <br /> Really though, this is just an example, to illustrate the possible space of structures around that the Lunars have to play with. Before the extreme of &quot;leaves in the forest&quot; you can play a bit more with spreading between more Attributes, but still having some primaries, and gating Charms after non-Craft focused Charms, but still having them mostly not.<br /> <br /> Everyone really has different views about the degree to which players playing a Lunar *should* be able to play a specialist in a similar area to an Ability. Though bear in mind the Abilities are basically selected to represent the primary types of interactions present in the heroic genre Exalted has, so how far do you really want to walk away from them, without messing with Lunar characters' ability to meaningfully contribute to Exalted stories? I'm probably more at the end of suspecting Lunars probably need to be able to specialize fairly robustly around specific applications to be engaging to play in a mixed Circle.<br /> <br /> (Parenthetically, I think there is also a difference between GSPs having, for'ex a Teleportation focused tree, which is built around that, or a Lunar having for'ex, a Strength tree. Teleportation is a specific kind of application, just an inhuman one that's at the edge of Exalted's genre one that does not have an Ability for it. Having a tree like that supports being a specialist with a good role to play in a group. A Strength tree doesn't seem quite the same thing, in that it could gives rise to a character who has a high general capacity, but might be much weaker at any specific application (covered by an Ability) than any character in the same Circle who has specialised along an application (Ability) based tree.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:52:39-07:00","id":1079909,"title":"","content":"Really though, it is more about a) are Lunars effective and fun characters to play (on a game level) and b) have Lunars been and are Lunars effective and cool characters to have in the wider Age of Sorrows and history of Creation (the setting level).<br /> <br /> Craft is kind of just one route to this ends, and piece in that puzzle, and if it ultimately, really, really, really whatever the writers try just doesn't fit their style, it isn't necessarily a failure state for Lunars.<br /> <br /> (To some degree I think late 2e made it feel like a failure state to not have much Craft, because the vibe there was a bit like &quot;Creation of the Age of Sorrows is a post apocalyptic magical sci-fi setting. The game is about rebuilding a technologically better world from the ruins of the apocalypse. So if you matter, you *need* to be doing serious technology&quot;. Craft as the route to technology became this big thing and this contentious thing.<br /> <br /> 3e's world, to the extent it carries that on (and it doesn't seem to as much), seems to have moved on to more emphasise sorcery over technology, and that as a space is more welcoming to character types that don't have a clear &quot;in&quot; to technology.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:05:59-07:00","id":1079919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079579#post1079579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Does</i> it?<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, just going with the base rules, <i>occasionally</i> producing wonders can be done with some combination of time, the right ingredients, and high dice pools, no fistful of Craft Charms or unique infrastructure required.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople have done the math on this, after all. The largest single obstacle to <i>mortals</i> making Artifacts is that it's just not an action they're permitted by the rules to take. (The second and third obstacles being the limited Terminus and the high difficulty, respectively.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just ran the numbers. To create an artifact, you need between 60 to 65 gxp, 5 to 10 sxp, the necessary materials, and an effective dice pool that depends on the artifact rating as follows: <br /> <br /> Rating Effective Dice Pool<br /> 2. 18<br /> 3. 25<br /> 4. 33<br /> 5. 42<br /> <br /> Based on the dice adder described in the back of the 3e book, a Lunar could hit the average number of dice for a level 2 artifact relatively easily (crafting usually requires either Dex or Int, so stunting to use both with your dice adder should be fairly simple) and could build a level 3 artifact if they spend WP and stunt well, but anything above that probably requires additional charms. While one could assert that anything Lunars have built that would be classed as Artifact 5+ was them attempting the same thing for a couple of decades until they got lucky, I'm pretty sure most players aren't going to even attempt something like that without a better chance of success.<br /> <br /> ....Well, ok, so they might attempt it, but when they fail after putting in two years of work, I'm betting they'll run the numbers and be discouraged and disappointed.<br /> <br /> Thus, while I don't know that forms Lunar Craft charms will take, it's fairly clear to me that they will have something more than just the dice adder.<br /> <br /> Edit: for anyone who wants to view my analysis in full, here's a link to the Google docs file: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18oDrfPnZVmHuYOa0-P48S5obA02GhAsOY3RsOM_mRzw\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...AsOY3RsOM_mRzw</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:17:08-07:00","id":1079925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079919#post1079919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the dice adder described in the back of the 3e book, a Lunar could hit the average number of dice for a level 2 artifact relatively easily (crafting usually requires either Dex or Int, so stunting to use both with your dice adder should be fairly simple) and could build a level 3 artifact if they spend WP and stunt well, but anything above that probably requires additional charms. While one could assert that anything Lunars have built that would be classed as <b>Artifact 5+</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are folks equating <a href=\"http://marvelcinematicuniverse.wikia.com/wiki/Iron_Man_Armor:_Mark_I\" target=\"_blank\">the armor Tony Stark built in a cave, with a box of scraps</a>, the one that fell apart a mere scene later, with a 5-dot Artifact? Would the five-dot suits not be the ones he later fabricated in his super-lab, with the aid of advanced machinery and supercomputers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:30:19-07:00","id":1079933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079925#post1079925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are folks equating <a href=\"http://marvelcinematicuniverse.wikia.com/wiki/Iron_Man_Armor:_Mark_I\" target=\"_blank\">the armor Tony Stark built in a cave, with a box of scraps</a>, the one that fell apart a mere scene later, with a 5-dot Artifact? Would the five-dot suits not be the ones he later fabricated in his super-lab, with the aid of advanced machinery and supercomputers?</div> </div> </div> </div>One might instead assume that an artificial Loom of Fate governing a massive western island is more likely to be in the 4-5 or N/A range than the 2-3 range, which means if Lunars are basically categorically incapable, with every bonus they can possibly gain adding to their roll, of creating this 4/5/N-A artifact, it throws into question whether they in fact did make it, or if it's just some Solar monolith they cavorted around, screeching and banging on with bones until it started working.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hope that they will get enough to make &quot;Lunar Artisan&quot; not a completely idiotic concept that is basically unplayable, while still keeping the pinnacle of craft from being something as casually reliable as Solars get it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:44:17-07:00","id":1079940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079933#post1079933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One might instead assume that an artificial Loom of Fate governing a massive western island is more likely to be in the 4-5 or N/A range than the 2-3 range...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and, just throwing it out there, maybe whatever's going on in the Caul is not the work of a single Lunar, and possibly not something expressed as a straightforward artifact?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079933#post1079933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which means if Lunars are basically categorically incapable, with every bonus they can possibly gain adding to their roll, of creating this 4/5/N-A artifact...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not talking about gathering every possible bonus to leverage for the roll; I was talking about <i>a cave and a box of scraps</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bPart of the problem is that most of the advantages that <i>would</i> give the Lunars the most crafting capabilities were and are part of the legacy of the First Age. Iron Man's story looks very different if he never gets to <i>leave </i>the desert; if instead of returning to the U.S. to spend billions of dollars in a sophisticated laboratory refining his armors and arc reactors, he had to wander the mountains under threat of constant manhunts, and scavenge for missile parts to maintain or improve on his armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079933#post1079933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it throws into question whether they in fact did make it, or if it's just some Solar monolith they cavorted around, screeching and banging on with bones until it started working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I expect this to change anything, but you're really not doing yourself any favors here by assuming that I want Lunars to just be a bunch of unthinking apes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2017, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T13:02:51-07:00","id":1079946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079940#post1079940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, and, just throwing it out there, maybe whatever's going on in the Caul is not the work of a single Lunar, and possibly not something expressed as a straightforward artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">A: <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></a></span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The Caul, the single biggest center of consolidated Lunar power, has been disconnected from the Loom of Fate. <b>Destiny there is controlled by an artifact constructed by the Lunars.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A simple artifact, maybe not, but it was previously defined as more artifact than simple sorcerous effect, and ideally, created by the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I don't expect it to be the work of a single Lunar. But unless they fudge the mechanics somehow and five Lunars can shapeshift together to create one Uber-Crafting Lunar who can manufacture with the equivalent of a 42-die pool, or they introduce sub-rules to get additional noncharm dice from assistance and other sources, a single Lunar [the project lead, essentially] still has to be making the 42-die-equivalent rolls listed above. And that's assuming its' only functionally crafted as a 5-dot. If it's a legendary project, it takes the equivalent of 76 dice, all told.<br /> <br /> It's thoroughly possible it's more Working than Craft, which does ease it up a bit [even if it's a Solar 2 working, it's significantly easier]. But, it was described as an artifact, created by the Lunars, which sets an upper boundary for what a fully invested Lunar craftsman is supposedly capable of, unless we're going to be told 'No, you're just not as smart as Makes-the-Caul, you'll never reach her level&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also my intent was not to assume you want that, only to point out what it feels like to be told &quot;You know this awesome thing Lunars made, they actually can't make it, ever. Presumably since they can't actually make it, they just found a Solar construction and pretended they made it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 04-17-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T13:24:08-07:00","id":1079954,"title":"","content":"Okay, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"756\" data-vbnamecard=\"756\">Meianno Yuurei</a> , please take these preconceptions of my point that you have in your head, and dump them out, because they really aren't helping. Nowhere did I say that Lunars can't make artifacts. In fact...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>I don't think it's a bad idea for Lunars to make artifacts.</b> I feel that they should be capable, in the best of circumstances, of pulling off some truly miraculous works of artifice. <i>Is that clear?</i><br /> <br /> Now, with that out of the way, Lunars have <i>not </i>been dealt the best of circumstances. At all. Between the scarcity of necessary materials (and not just magical ones like behemoth fangs, but even stuff like bronze), the threat of the Wyld Hunt, the lack of First Age laboratories and such, Lunars are in a bad way when it comes to crafting. They might be particularly well-suited among their Exalted peers to thrive in those circumstances, but it's still a poor position to be thrust into.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the subject of how the Caul was made, I don't think it's necessary to pick apart the story of its creation any more than folks need to sit down and calculate how Rakan Thulio parried the Mark of Saturn, so let's pretend we're talking about just making a wonder of similar power.<br /> <br /> Now, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said: playing with the craft XP or altering the terminus is probably outside their wheelhouse. But that hardly removes every possibility! Consider dice tricks. Or stunt enhancers. Or reroll effects. Or any number of other options. These will not be given a similar cost as a Solar artisan's Charms, but they hardly need to be for a five-dot artifact to be within the realm of possibility (albeit hardly incentivized).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T13:45:14-07:00","id":1079967,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve found that the base craft system offers an excellent workaround for its problems. If you ignore the craft system as written and develop your own, sensible system then that seems to fix most of the craft problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:20:10-07:00","id":1079991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079954#post1079954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said: playing with the craft XP or altering the terminus is probably outside their wheelhouse. But that hardly removes every possibility! Consider dice tricks. Or stunt enhancers. Or reroll effects. Or any number of other options. These will not be given a similar cost as a Solar artisan's Charms, but they hardly need to be for a five-dot artifact to be within the realm of possibility (albeit hardly incentivized).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more or less my suspicion, that Lunars will have trouble generating white XP or sidestepping the actual systems of Craft, but will also have the opportunity and potential to match (or nearly match, or shit, I could even see them exceeding if both have a small amount of investment) the Solar Exalted in terms of raw power.<br /> <br /> This would have the side-effect of making the Lunar Exalted quite good at manufacturing the artifice common to the Age of Sorrows: Daiklaves, Essence Gliders, and so on, but cause trouble with First Age artifice like Warstriders or Airships, or Looms of Fate, without making these impossible for them to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","user":"nihnoz","date":". 04-17-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:30:15-07:00","id":1079997,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind that a relative lack of materials, elaborate workshops, and support networks will also make trouble for their crafting (though probably not as drastically for them as lacks of such might be for other splats!). Unlike Solars, they can't just Wyld-Shape for orichalcum; unlike Dragon-Blooded, they're not perched on the bones of the greatest empire in the world, with further support and supplies from countless city-states; unlike the Sidereals, Abyssals, and Infernals, they don't have the largesse of gods, Deathlords, and demon princes, or the splendor of Heaven, the Underworld, or Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:35:38-07:00","id":1080004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079967#post1079967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve found that the base craft system offers an excellent workaround for its problems. If you ignore the craft system as written and develop your own, sensible system then that seems to fix most of the craft problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDon't be cute, Lemon, you're too old for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:00:00-07:00","id":1080028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079925#post1079925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are folks equating <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://marvelcinematicuniverse.wikia.com/wiki/Iron_Man_Armor:_Mark_I&amp;quot;]the</a> armor Tony Stark built in a cave, with a box of scraps[/URL], the one that fell apart a mere scene later, with a 5-dot Artifact? Would the five-dot suits not be the ones he later fabricated in his super-lab, with the aid of advanced machinery and supercomputers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't. I was asserting that some Lunars, either individually or together, had created artifacts of rank 5+ before and thus have to have some kind of craft charms to make creating those things move from the &quot;mathematically impossible&quot; arena to the &quot;heroic achievement&quot; arena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:05:59-07:00","id":1080031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080028#post1080028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't. I was asserting that some Lunars, either individually or together, had created artifacts of rank 5+ before...</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 5 is shifting the goalposts, though - the OP specifically was talking about making amazing things, not earth-shaking ones. He - and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar84_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"84\" data-vbnamecard=\"84\">Holden</a> before him - even used the &quot;in a cave, with a box of scraps&quot; bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2017, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:14:24-07:00","id":1080034,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, if I was going to guess what craft charm Lunars DON'T get, I'd say it was Thousand Forge Hands. Because that's the &quot;you don't need infrastructure to make artifacts&quot; charm. Without that charm or some equivalent, any Lunar that wants to build a rank 4+ artifact is going to be sitting in their cave, working with their box of scraps for over a year. I find it hard to credit that the Wyld Hunt would leave them alone for that entire time, unless said Lunar was hella far away from the Realm and/or incredibly well hidden (and I'm not sure you can hide that well from the Sids).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:22:57-07:00","id":1080040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080031#post1080031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 5 is shifting the goalposts, though - the OP specifically was talking about making amazing things, not earth-shaking ones. He - and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> before him - even used the &amp;quot;in a cave, with a box of scraps&amp;quot; bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. Going back over this thread I thought your argument was &quot;Even mortals have enough dice to make artifacts, so Lunars don't need Craft charms&quot; and I was responding by pointing out that &quot;No, mortals don't get enough dice to create rank 3+ artifacts and, as is, Lunars don't get enough dice to make rank 4+ Artifacts, and, since Lunars HAVE built such wonders in setting, they do need Craft charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, from rereading this thread and your responses, it sounds like we don't actually disagree on this point or at least not in the way I thought. I'm sorry for mischaracterizing your argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:23:00-07:00","id":1080041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080034#post1080034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it hard to credit that the Wyld Hunt would leave them alone for that entire time, unless said Lunar was hella far away from the Realm and/or incredibly well hidden (and I'm not sure you can hide that well from the Sids).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of Lunars who are not going to be hiding in this edition. At all. Lunars rule non-trivial parts of Creation openly as kings and potentates.<br /> <br /> One of them is in the corebook, even! Jyudo Far-Flung rules a large territory that abuts a major Realm satrapy from his manse, in which he has amassed a great library. The Realm and the Sidereals 100% know he's there, they just<i> can't get him out. </i>They've tried. It didn't go so well.<br /> <br /> Jyudo doesn't seem like he's all that interested in doing something like forging a daiklave, but I'd argue that a Lunar in his position absolutely has the time and resources to do so assuming their essence can be bent to that project with any facility at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:44:14-07:00","id":1080050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080034#post1080034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it, if I was going to guess what craft charm Lunars DON'T get, I'd say it was Thousand Forge Hands. Because that's the &quot;you don't need infrastructure to make artifacts&quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we thinking about the same Charm?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Exalt\u2019s hands flow with the Essence of a thousand craftsmen; her urge is legion and her well is bottomless. When she creates a superior or legendary slot, she may use this Charm to greatly speed her efforts to begin the project (p. 239). This may be represented as the Exalt thinking, planning, and working with impossible speed. Though it cannot dictate the speed at which she gathers materials or performs tasks not directly associated with Craft, this Charm guarantees that given all such materials are provided, and all such tasks have been completed, the design and forging work that comes before she can roll to finish takes no longer than (6 - Essence) months for N/A and five dot Artifacts, and no more than (6 - Essence) weeks for all else.&quot;<br /> <br /> THAT Charm?<br /> <br /> Thousand Forge Hands does absolutely nothing to alleviate your needs for infrastructure; it demands that you have everything you need to begin, and then simply lets you get the job done quickly.<br /> <br /> Given that the effect is fluffed as a matter of planning and speed, I think a reduced version is perfectly acceptable for Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4742_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4742\" data-vbnamecard=\"4742\">Murcushio</a> has already refuted your other point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T16:17:43-07:00","id":1080059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079954#post1079954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said: playing with the craft XP or altering the terminus is probably outside their wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree about the terminus, but I would like you to share your logic regarding craft XP.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to reward Lunar Exalted for the crafting they've already done while also encouraging them to not do so much crafting in the future, giving them a version of Spirit-Stoking Elevation seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've gone through the entire Solar Craft Charmset, and out of that <i>massive </i>tower I've identified only six or seven Solar Charms that I think Lunar Exalted could have with minor alteration.<br /> <br /> <i>Spirit-Stoking Elevation</i>, for the reason I just gave.<br /> <br /> <i>Thousand Forge Hands</i>, because as I already pointed out to BrilliantRain, it represents planning and speed. But it doesn't need to be NEARLY as fast as the Solar Charm, especially as it would preferably work as a <i>general </i>&quot;plan faster&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> Likewise, <i>Copper Spider Conception</i>, which is also fluffed as good forward planning, and which is valuable to Lunars who aren't looking to make Artifacts but who still want to create mundane structures with mundane superior project slots.<br /> <br /> <i>Arete-Shifting Prana</i>, because Lunar Exalted are adaptable. Also, because they're FUCKED when it comes to buying up multiple Craft abilities, and without the other Charms that Solars get regarding maxed-out Craft Ability ratings, this would hardly break anything. If necessary, limit this Charm to affecting only Craft Abilities that deal with organic materials, like Leatherworking, Cooking, and Medicine-making. Possibly also let it key off of (or boost) your actual Medicine rating, as you use your Sewing skills to stitch up someone's wounds or your cooking skills to nurse someone back to health.<br /> <br /> <i>Tireless Workhorse Method</i> is too focused on crafting for Lunars, and too good at it. I think a Lunar version would grant, AT MOST, only one Major project slot per Essence. In return, whenever the Lunar isn't using that Major slot for anything, he reduces penalties related to multitasking. Which, of course, incentivizes the Lunar to not use the Charm for crafting at all unless he really, really needs to.<br /> <br /> <i>Shattering Grasp</i>, because the Lunar Exalted have always had Charms for breaking stuff, which I want to advance into a Charm for digging more quickly through solid stone obstructions too thick to be called &quot;walls&quot;; like entire mountains.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for other crafting XP tricks, instead of things like Brass Scales Falling, Red Anvils Ringing, or Chains Fall Away, the Lunar would get more crafting XP when they fashion trophies and tools out of the corpse of something whose Heart's Blood they took... or that the intended recipient took.<br /> <br /> <br /> Outside of that? I don't see a single Solar Crafting Charm that I think looks appropriate for the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-17-2017, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T19:12:02-07:00","id":1080137,"title":"","content":"Here's an example of one of my ideas. I tried to balance it against the Extra Limbs Merit. It's probably shit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Diligent Hive Imitation \u2013 Lunars are excellent multitaskers, as capable of juggling many thoughts as a hive is capable of handling separate simultaneous tasks.</b><br /> <i>Cost: 5m;</i><br /> <i>Mins: Intelligence 2, Essence 1; Type: Simple:</i><br /> <i>Keywords: Mute; Duration: Indefinite;</i><br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms: None</i><br /> <br /> As long as this Charm is in effect, the Lunar effectively has another major project slot for crafting. However, if he is not currently using that slot, this Charm grants an alternative bonus for combat: When the character performs a flurry, one of her actions (of the player\u2019s choice) suffers only a -1 rather than a -3 penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> An alternative that I could be happy with is that this Charm, instead, reduces the penalty for Miscellaneous actions alone. Thus does a Lunar who learns a crafting Charm become more capable of rapidly fixing or cobbling together a necessary doodad or bandaging up an ally's bleeding wounds in the middle of a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-17-2017, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T03:35:56-07:00","id":1080231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080059#post1080059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree about the terminus, but I would like you to share your logic regarding craft XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually, reading this first line of your post, I am suddenly struck with the notion that Charms for crafting experience could actually serve as a good means of incentivizing one to craft down particular routes by creating custom craft objectives. Say for Abyssals, rather than &quot;this is a Solar Crafting Charm, but it only works for making things that kill, so it's technically inferior&quot;, you get &quot;in addition to the usual objectives, you get more crafting experience for making something that fulfils the chivalry of death or some Old Law of the Underworld&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I could see something similar for Lunars; not an across the board enhancement, but something that leads into the characterization of the Lunar Exalted by making the conditions that they craft in and the purposes that they craft for something that their Charms make easier, in a manner more organic than only getting dice bonuses or tricks when they make specific things.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also occurs to me that such a thing could lead into distinct Lunar narratives for the creation of legendary projects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:16:30-07:00","id":1080255,"title":"","content":"I would like to see Lunars being able to do amazing stuff with limited resources and be able to do great when it comes to quickly coming up with something usable or maintenance, but have a much harder time when it comes to pumping out world-shattering artefacts or huge monolithic structures. What if their charms just don\u00b4t give as much support to the higher-end project slots and focus on being able to do serviceable stuff quickly and from limited and normally unsuitable resources? Sure, it might be harder to make legendary projects than it is for Solars (and maybe even large groups of Dragonborns) - for that, perhaps there would be charms that make it possible, but in a more roundabout way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 04-18-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:14:11-07:00","id":1080325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080231#post1080231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bActually, reading this first line of your post, I am suddenly struck with the notion that Charms for crafting experience could actually serve as a good means of incentivizing one to craft down particular routes by creating custom craft objectives. Say for Abyssals, rather than &quot;this is a Solar Crafting Charm, but it only works for making things that kill, so it's technically inferior&quot;, you get &quot;in addition to the usual objectives, you get more crafting experience for making something that fulfils the chivalry of death or some Old Law of the Underworld&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I could see something similar for Lunars; not an across the board enhancement, but something that leads into the characterization of the Lunar Exalted by making the conditions that they craft in and the purposes that they craft for something that their Charms make easier, in a manner more organic than only getting dice bonuses or tricks when they make specific things.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also occurs to me that such a thing could lead into distinct Lunar narratives for the creation of legendary projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted get crafting XP in exactly the same ways everyone else does... but MORE, and without any selective weight given to any particular basic objective.<br /> <br /> Other Exalted can get crafting XP in ways no one else can, and reward certain basic objectives more than others, especially by meeting ever-more-specific conditions. They can also get their own unique ways to spend crafting XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if Lunars could earn <i>and</i> spend craft XP for healing others or for planning a heist, but that it required filling a Major or Superior project slot for the effort? That certainly encourages them to do various clever and useful things besides crafting!<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, I want to explore the possibility of putting analogues of Copper Spider Conception and Thousand Forge Hands into a general &quot;forward-thinking / master planning&quot; Intelligence Charm tree that allows Lunar Exalted to &quot;prepare for success&quot;. It doesn't have a focus on building artifacts the way that Solar Craft does, but instead revolves around removing obstacles and providing solutions to much more common problems.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see this Charm include effects like Stealth-based Stalking Shadow Spirit (scope out a location to find the best hiding spots), Larceny-based Master Plan Meditation and Sun-Stealing Shadow Spirit, and Craft-based Ever-Ready Innovation Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:54:26-07:00","id":1080466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1079967#post1079967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve found that the base craft system offers an excellent workaround for its problems. If you ignore the craft system as written and develop your own, sensible system then that seems to fix most of the craft problems.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This isn't really relevant to the conversation and is arguably threadcrapping. Please avoid making posts like this in the future, it isn't conducive to having a good conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:05:28-07:00","id":1080472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1080231#post1080231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bActually, reading this first line of your post, I am suddenly struck with the notion that Charms for crafting experience could actually serve as a good means of incentivizing one to craft down particular routes by creating custom craft objectives. Say for Abyssals, rather than &quot;this is a Solar Crafting Charm, but it only works for making things that kill, so it's technically inferior&quot;, you get &quot;in addition to the usual objectives, you get more crafting experience for making something that fulfils the chivalry of death or some Old Law of the Underworld&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I could see something similar for Lunars; not an across the board enhancement, but something that leads into the characterization of the Lunar Exalted by making the conditions that they craft in and the purposes that they craft for something that their Charms make easier, in a manner more organic than only getting dice bonuses or tricks when they make specific things.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also occurs to me that such a thing could lead into distinct Lunar narratives for the creation of legendary projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely something I'd like to see for a number of splats' craft charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:28:37-07:00","id":1080626,"title":"","content":"&quot;Craft-XP&quot; Charms should especially reward Lunar Exalted for making:<br /> <br /> * disguises; essentially a basic craft project<br /> * forgeries and counterfeits<br /> * traps<br /> * hiding spaces<br /> <br /> The Lunar labor / planning / crafting Charm tree should start with encouraging Lunar Exalted who are interested in that path to start casing out every place they intend to infiltrate, attack, defend, or otherwise confront others. Get Lunars to scope out the possible hiding spots, so that they can hide there or know where to look for stealthy enemies. Get Lunars to make their own hiding spots. Get Lunars to lay traps everywhere.<br /> <br /> Do you really need a shiny daiklaive when a simple spike-laden pit-trap will do the job? Stack the deck! Change the rules! Fight dirty!<br /> <br /> It's only after you've mastered the art of planning ahead and preparing with cheap, mundane tools that you can start planning and preparing better for the creation of Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:58:56-07:00","id":1080647,"title":"","content":"<b>PLAYING TRICKS</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>\u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Intelligence 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>???<br /> This Charm expands the number of actions which count as basic crafting projects for the purpose of earning the Exalt silver crafting experience; these projects now include Larceny actions to create forgeries, counterfeits, disguises, and the concealment of evidence. The Lunar further earns an additional silver point for every basic objective she fulfills by producing such things, as well as producing hiding places, traps, and objects which are booby-trapped, poisonous, or otherwise hiding an unpleasant surprise.<br /> <br /> Inspiring a character to develop or increase a negative Intimacy for the Lunar, such as due to being tricked, explicitly counts as a basic objective, and the Lunar counts that as a separate condition from any positive Intimacy he inspires or increases in a different character with the same project. Even if both Intimacies are within the same character; it is not unknown for the Lunar Exalted to earn the respect as well as the hatred of those they foil, and such relationships are often the stuff of legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:32:57-07:00","id":1081160,"title":"","content":"Continuing this trend of &quot;Lunar Intelligence favors those who plan ahead&quot;...<br /> <br /> Where Holistic Battle Understanding allows a Solar to continue performing at his best even when completely unfamiliar with the opposing forces or its generals, the Lunar Charm could reward the Lunar Exalt for preparing ahead of time by converting the bonus dice for familiarity into bonus successes.<br /> <br /> This further encourages Lunar commanders to steal out in the middle of the night as a bird or mouse, spying on the enemy and sabotaging their logistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:49:47-07:00","id":1081437,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'm not sure about that. I feel that actually planning is more something in the Solar thematic set. Lunars are adaptable; they should be able to do fine without planning.<br /> <br /> Except maybe plans that involve the natural environment, like leading your enemies into a nest of poisonous snakes, I could something like that going on.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I don't think Lunars need encouragement to go and spy and sabotage; they're great at it, so they nearly always will, probably more than Solars.<br /> <br /> As to the extra craft objectives, what do you think about objectives related to materials? Like, things made out of animal parts (bones, furs, etc). That's something I remember someone suggested before.<br /> <br /> Also, as well as making booby-traps, how about something about making things that help adapt to an environment?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:59:13-07:00","id":1081441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1081437#post1081437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except maybe plans that involve the natural environment, like leading your enemies into a nest of poisonous snakes, I could something like that going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this makes Lunars out to be too literally the &quot;animal exalted&quot;. They aren't (only) the Exalted of wilderness. They are adaptable, and not just in the way that animals are adaptable. They should be able to function (and plan) just as well within a city than within a forest or a desert. Seven Devil Clever's Charms shouldn't be penalized for being in an aristocratic milieu, for example.<br /> <br /> I remember there being discussion about having a sort of predatory intuitive intelligence, like the Alien, where you understand the purpose of things and the reactions of people without necessarily knowing anything about those things/people. That could be an interesting seed for this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-20-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T08:12:49-07:00","id":1081443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1081437#post1081437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I'm not sure about that. I feel that actually planning is more something in the Solar thematic set. Lunars are adaptable; they should be able to do fine without planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what their non-Intelligence Charms would be for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except maybe plans that involve the natural environment, like leading your enemies into a nest of poisonous snakes, I could something like that going on. </div> </div> </div>I agree with Fata-Ku's rebuttal; this makes no logical or thematic sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And honestly, I don't think Lunars need encouragement to go and spy and sabotage; they're great at it, so they nearly always will, probably more than Solars. </div> </div> </div>You could say the same thing about Solar Crafters. Why do they have so many crafting XP Charms to encourage them to go out and craft anything and everything when they're already so good at getting crafting XP by crafting lots of things very quickly?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the extra craft objectives, what do you think about objectives related to materials? Like, things made out of animal parts (bones, furs, etc). That's something I remember someone suggested before. </div> </div> </div>That's been me the whole time, and I did think about it.<br /> <br /> However, I think &quot;make things out of organic materials&quot; as an avenue for additional crafting experience is too easily abused considering that it can be stacked with other objective-enhancing Charms.<br /> <br /> So, while &quot;making things out of your Heart's Blood kills&quot; should be a new basic object, Shaping The Once-Living Form should instead look to make you BETTER at working with organic material, rather than rewarding you for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, as well as making booby-traps, how about something about making things that help adapt to an environment? </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea, but you're going to need to get more specific and illustrative than that.<br /> <br /> <i>Weapons</i> help one adapt to an environment, for example.<br /> <br /> What I currently have in mind is one Charm that rewards a Lunar more for constructing shelters, and another Charm that makes them better at doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to tie Lunar Charms for breaking objects into Charms for digging, and then perhaps to working the earth to prepare it for architecture. Essentially adding &quot;dirt and stone&quot; to &quot;organic materials&quot; for the list of things Lunars can craft better, if not using exactly the same mechanics.<br /> <br /> Call it, &quot;Earth and Moon Blessing&quot;, stealing from that Second Edition Charm that let Lunars shapeshift into landscape features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-20-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:24:17-07:00","id":1083077,"title":"","content":"Sorry to possibly chime in with an irrelevant point that I've probably missed, but wouldn't Craftsman Needs No Tools be a perfect Lunar charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:12:57-07:00","id":1083095,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:16:05-07:00","id":1083097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083077#post1083077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to possibly chime in with an irrelevant point that I've probably missed, but wouldn't Craftsman Needs No Tools be a perfect Lunar charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember if it made it to 2e, but in 1e they had a similar Charm, in which with a little shapeshifting they could use their bodyparts as tools (claws as saws and chisels, fists as hammers, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T18:44:17-07:00","id":1083257,"title":"","content":"Treating their flesh and bones as hammers and chisels sounds more like the grisly and visceral Liminal Exalted, who control the meaty, blood materials of corporeal bodies.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted are celestial Exalted, reborn through reincarnating divine souls. Their power is very internal, and gives them the power to shape their minds and souls. It's in becoming Lunar Exalted that their souls grow to include a Totem and Spirit Shape.<br /> <br /> A difficulty with projecting power externally is why we're unlikely to see Glorious LUNAR Saber and the like. I don't think they can just conjure up craftsman's tools from Essence, either. Deadly Beastman Transformation focuses their power even further inward, reducing their ability to Evoke power from Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T20:03:08-07:00","id":1083287,"title":"","content":"I would imagine the Lunar pouring a bit of blood on the raw materials, or otherwise imbuing it with his power, in order to imbue the materials with a portion of his own malleability, allowing him to sculpt it into whatever form he wants. The effect would be, &quot;The Lunar can Craft without tools&quot; but not because he has any tool of the job (like the Solar) but rather due too the way the Lunar changes the material in question, so it doesn't need to be worked by tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T20:10:16-07:00","id":1083290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083287#post1083287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine the Lunar pouring a bit of blood on the raw materials, or otherwise imbuing it with his power, in order to imbue the materials with a portion of his own malleability, allowing him to sculpt it into whatever form he wants. The effect would be, &quot;The Lunar can Craft without tools&quot; but not because he has any tool of the job (like the Solar) but rather due too the way the Lunar changes the material in question, so it doesn't need to be worked by tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar idea, and it seems like a great thing to give the name &quot;Clay Wetting Practice&quot;, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> hated the idea for some reason I don't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T21:49:24-07:00","id":1083338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083290#post1083290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a similar idea, and it seems like a great thing to give the name &quot;Clay Wetting Practice&quot;, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> hated the idea for some reason I don't remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>It externalizes the internal power of shapeshifting in an extremely generic fashion and reminds me of the Wyld Exalted era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T01:04:36-07:00","id":1083886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083257#post1083257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they can just conjure up craftsman's tools from Essence, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bStrictly speaking, that's not the aesthetic ascribed to Craftsman Needs No Tools.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor a Lunar crafting Charm of such potence, I wouldn't ascribe it to shapeshifting or to making the subject malleable, but to an act in their more trickster functions, a result of being quick and clever.<br /> <br /> \u200bPossibly, one detail that could distinguish it from Solar Charms could be that crafting in such a manner waives the natural experience that they gain out of it.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I've come down on Charms that define a limit to what you can craft, but I'm wondering if something that would follow the idea of being able to work quickly based on drawing a unique insight out of desperate situations, putting together something that can get you out of it and then going, might be fitting and functional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:39:26-07:00","id":1083965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083338#post1083338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It externalizes the internal power of shapeshifting in an extremely generic fashion and reminds me of the Wyld Exalted era.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, do you think the Lunar Exalted are going to lose the Charms they have for transforming other people into their Heart's Blood shapes?<br /> <br /> Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique, and Insidious Lunar Transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:59:11-07:00","id":1083970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083965#post1083965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think the Lunar Exalted are going to lose the Charms they have for transforming other people into their Heart's Blood shapes?<br /> <br /> Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique, and Insidious Lunar Transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those, with their particular aesthetics, limitations, and themes, probably have a better chance of staying than a Charm that was first described as working through working Wyld Essence into something. After all, doppleganger stories often have the copied individual turn into someone else while the doppleganger has their form, and then you have that whole Curse of the Wolf deal to force on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:09:43-07:00","id":1083978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083970#post1083970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those, with their particular aesthetics, limitations, and themes, probably have a better chance of staying than a Charm that was first described as working through working Wyld Essence into something. After all, doppleganger stories often have the copied individual turn into someone else while the doppleganger has their form, and then you have that whole Curse of the Wolf deal to force on others.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Lunars can feed their blood to others to transform them, I think Lunars can soak their blood into objects made of organic material to reanimate them enough that their healing process assists the Lunar's ability to repair them.<br /> <br /> It would also be neat if a Lunar could use this trick to transform any common hide and bone into copies of the rare hide and bone of some magical monster whose Blood he stole. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't object if this trick could be bent towards easing the difficulty of crafting things made of hide, bone, and wood. <br /> <br /> At no point does the Wyld enter into the picture. Just the transformative Essence of the Lunar Exalted, externalized through the same medium by which they internalize the Essence of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:47:54-07:00","id":1083991,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about this, and trying to render it in light of how the Solar charmset handles some things as genre tricks.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a no moon oracle who uses his insight to find whatever is missing in a Craftsman's work: a sacrifice that must be made, an insight they lack, or what-have-you. Maybe they use it for their own handiwork, but an elder often finds this to be another bit of the wisdom that others prize in him.<br /> <br /> I see where Sunder is going with his &quot;imbue materials with the qualities of a behemoth in your library&quot; charm. I'm a little iffy on this, if only because I feel like that can reduce the significance of those hard to find components.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to let a Lunar do something *like* this, but it would be a &quot;once a season&quot; thing on the low end, and I'd honestly strongly consider &quot;costs you the behemoth's shape&quot; as part of the cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:56:55-07:00","id":1083995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083991#post1083991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where Sunder is going with his &quot;imbue materials with the qualities of a behemoth in your library&quot; charm. I'm a little iffy on this, if only because I feel like that can reduce the significance of those hard to find components.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to let a Lunar do something *like* this, but it would be a &quot;once a season&quot; thing on the low end, and I'd honestly strongly consider &quot;costs you the behemoth's shape&quot; as part of the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a steep cost for an effect that is really only sparing the Lunar of the trial of skinning or deboning himself and regenerating the damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:04:50-07:00","id":1083999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083995#post1083995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's a steep cost for an effect that is really only sparing the Lunar of the trial of skinning or deboning himself and regenerating the damage.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How is ripping off pieces of oneself to make Artifacts <i>more</i> Lunar-appropriate than Tool-Hand Technique?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:17:24-07:00","id":1084003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083995#post1083995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a steep cost for an effect that is really only sparing the Lunar of the trial of skinning or deboning himself and regenerating the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to regard behemoths as unique entities. Imbuing something with the physical and spiritual qualities of a one-of-a-kind terror that has been long deceased is, IMHO, a big deal.<br /> <br /> (I would frankly consider materials from the shapeshifted lunar subpar in this regard: they would still have whatever physical strengths the original hide and/or bone might possess, but the essential nature of it would be the Exalt's rather than the original creature's.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:45:20-07:00","id":1084019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083999#post1083999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is ripping off pieces of oneself to make Artifacts <i>more</i> Lunar-appropriate than Tool-Hand Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div>Skinning things, including yourself, is &quot;barbaric&quot;, for one thing.<br /> <br /> How barbaric or bestial is forming your hand into a crescent wrench or screwdriver of flesh and bone? That image clashes horribly with the Lunar aesthetic, whereas that kind of irreverence for one's body is perfect for Liminal Exalted.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:55:46-07:00","id":1084026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084019#post1084019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skinning things, including yourself, is &amp;quot;barbaric&amp;quot;, for one thing.<br /> <br /> How barbaric or bestial is forming your hand into a crescent wrench or screwdriver of flesh and bone? That image clashes horribly with the Lunar aesthetic, whereas that kind of irreverence for one's body is perfect for Liminal Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>THT doesn't literally shapeshift your hand into a tool. It enhances existing features. Your fist stays a fist, it's just reinforced to punch in nails. Your claws stay claws, they're just sharpened for climbing or sawing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:03:43-07:00","id":1084035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084026#post1084026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THT doesn't literally shapeshift your hand into a tool. It enhances existing features. Your fist stays a fist, it's just reinforced to punch in nails. Your claws stay claws, they're just sharpened for climbing or sawing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it sounds like Tool-Hand Technique should follow <i>after </i>Body-Weapon Technique. The trick you propose starts with a foundation of making your natural weapons sharper and harder before it progresses to the point of using them more cleverly.<br /> <br /> The difficulty then becomes crossing Attributes, as Body-Weapon Technique should be Strength-based (and if not that, then Stamina-based), whereas Tool-Hand Technique's cleverness would be Dexterity or Intelligence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:03:52-07:00","id":1084036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084026#post1084026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THT doesn't literally shapeshift your hand into a tool. It enhances existing features. Your fist stays a fist, it's just reinforced to punch in nails. Your claws stay claws, they're just sharpened for climbing or sawing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original form of the Charm had a bizarre description where your hand did take on features of a tool. It doesn't really need to do that if you already have claws, thick knuckles, or the like, but 1e gotta 1e and lead into 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:07:47-07:00","id":1084041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084036#post1084036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original form of the Charm had a bizarre description where your hand did take on features of a tool. It doesn't really need to do that if you already have claws, thick knuckles, or the like, but 1e gotta 1e and lead into 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to forget that and move on if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar43_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"43\" data-vbnamecard=\"43\">Fata-Ku</a> or anyone else can provide a solution to the cross-Attribute problem of Body-Weapon Technique -&gt; Tool-Hand Technique.<br /> <br /> I would further expand upon Tool-Hand Technique so that it becomes more effective depending on the size of your Heart's Blood Library, to represent the sheer variety of claw sizes and beak shapes, poisons, web-silks, and other features that the Lunar can employ as a toolbox.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if Tool-Hand Technique <i>didn't</i> follow after Body-Weapon Technique, but it still needed Body-Weapon Technique to reach its full potential? The Lunar can still use claws as tools, but those tools only work for Minor projects; using them for Major projects would require also using Body-Weapon Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:58:13-07:00","id":1084064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084036#post1084036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original form of the Charm had a bizarre description where your hand did take on features of a tool. It doesn't really need to do that if you already have claws, thick knuckles, or the like, but 1e gotta 1e and lead into 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really? it just says it strengthens hands and sharpens claws, and gives them a superficial resemblance. It <i>can</i> be taken to mean shapeshifting, but it can also just mean &quot;you make a screwdriver shape with your hand&quot; without involving shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084041#post1084041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to forget that and move on if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar43_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"43\" data-vbnamecard=\"43\">Fata-Ku</a> or anyone else can provide a solution to the cross-Attribute problem of Body-Weapon Technique -&gt; Tool-Hand Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find the 2e version (does it even exist? Exalted wiki has only the 1e version), so I'm not sure what problem you're talking about. 1e THT came out of Shaping the Ideal Form and had no relation to Body Weapon Technique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would further expand upon Tool-Hand Technique so that it becomes more effective depending on the size of your Heart's Blood Library, to represent the sheer variety of claw sizes and beak shapes, poisons, web-silks, and other features that the Lunar can employ as a toolbox.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if Tool-Hand Technique <i>didn't</i> follow after Body-Weapon Technique, but it still needed Body-Weapon Technique to reach its full potential? The Lunar can still use claws as tools, but those tools only work for Minor projects; using them for Major projects would require also using Body-Weapon Technique. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd keep them completely separate, aside from maybe a synergy where having WBT allows THT to &quot;create&quot; Exceptional Tools (thus granting the tool bonus) and allowing it to work on Superior projects (as much as mundane exceptional tools could, anyway) \u2013 I think making only work on basic projects is too heavy a limitation. I think it's fair to allow it to make Combat-ready weapons, which are Major.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:07:41-07:00","id":1084068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084064#post1084064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find the 2e version (does it even exist? Exalted wiki has only the 1e version), so I'm not sure what problem you're talking about. 1e THT came out of Shaping the Ideal Form and had no relation to Weapon Body Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>There never was a relationship before, but going forward, there logically should be. If a Lunar can make his hand hard enough to serve as a hammer, that's the conceptual space of Body-Weapon Technique. Using that hammer to craft is the following conceptual space occupied by Tool-Hand Technique.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I'd keep them completely separate, aside from maybe a synergy where having WBT allows THT to &quot;create&quot; Exceptional Tools and allowing it to work on superior projects \u2013 I think making only work on basic projects is too heavy a limitation. I think it's fair to allow it to make Combat-ready weapons, which are Major. </div> </div> </div>You should be aware that Craftsman Needs No Tools is not permitted to assist with crafting artifacts, or perhaps Superior projects in general. Which makes sense for mundane superior projects, where a Solar should be more in need of workmen than an individual set of tools.<br /> <br /> Combat-ready weapons include sharp sticks with stones tied to the ends. Wooden planks with bits of obsidian shards or shark-teeth poking out of the business ends. Throwing-slings made of leather. Bolas made of rope and rocks.<br /> <br /> Requiring two entry-level Charms to have tools for working on major projects is just fine, especially when one of those Charms enhances Lunar combat prowess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:28:10-07:00","id":1084077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084068#post1084068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There never was a relationship before, but going forward, there logically should be. If a Lunar can make his hand hard enough to serve as a hammer, that's the conceptual space of Body-Weapon Technique. Using that hammer to craft is the following conceptual space occupied by Tool-Hand Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok, I misread your intention there, sorry.<br /> In that case I think it'd be more appropriate to learn to make tools from your hands before making weapons. It feels more like a progression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You should be aware that Craftsman Needs No Tools is not permitted to assist with crafting artifacts, or perhaps Superior projects in general. Which makes sense for mundane superior projects, where a Solar should be more in need of workmen than an individual set of tools. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combat-ready weapons include sharp sticks with stones tied to the ends. Wooden planks with bits of obsidian shards or shark-teeth poking out of the business ends. Throwing-slings made of leather. Bolas made of rope and rocks. </div> </div> </div>Thing is, the Charm itself is already intrinsically more limited than CNNT in that you're still working as though you had tools, you're not e.g. shaping steel as though it was clay as CNNT, you still need a source of heat and still need to pound it for hours. Taking it down yet another notch just for the sake of it seems entirely unnecessary to me. Just because Lunars have a barbarian aesthetic doesn't mean they're limited to the stone-age in everything they do.<br /> <br /> Because then there's also a matter of &quot;well, if it can make a hammer to forge a steel arrow-head, why can't it make a hammer to forge a steel sword?&quot;<br /> The exception of Superior Projects is simpler: it doesn't make your fist hard enough to pound orichalcum/jade/whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Requiring two entry-level Charms to have tools for working on major projects is just fine, especially when one of those Charms enhances Lunar combat prowess.</span> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it shouldn't have pre-requisites. I'm essentially fine with having it be the 2nd or 3rd in the tree (as it was in 1e). Rather I'm just really not fond of WBT, especially now that its only benefit is adding the Lethal tag to what's otherwise the stats of every Light Weapon. If instead WBT followed THT, I think it'd benefit WBT by allowing it to be more interesting \u2013 adding tags or maybe even getting Medium Weapon fists.<br /> { Edit: I can see this working to the benefit of their theme: &quot;His strikes were as [Flexible] as a cobra!&quot;, said about adding the Flexible tag to one's punches. }<br /> <br /> Perhaps it could have a few more paths to it? I could see Strength and Dex allowing access to it as much as ... wait... it was Manipulation?? wat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:45:56-07:00","id":1084105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084064#post1084064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, not really? it just says it strengthens hands and sharpens claws, and gives them a superficial resemblance. It <i>can</i> be taken to mean shapeshifting, but it can also just mean &quot;you make a screwdriver shape with your hand&quot; without involving shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first part of the Charm makes it sound like it's noticeably less superficial and involves definite shapeshifting. But then, it wouldn't be the first time that a Lunar Charm's text ended up horribly mangled and at odds with itself. Flowing Body Evasion, after all, didn't even tell you if it actually stopped undodgeable or perfect attacks, what the Charm actually looked like, and it went on for like half a page when it was saying nothing.<br /> <br /> And it was Simple type and based on Charisma. The salt floe never ends for FBE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-26-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:10:27-07:00","id":1084118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084105#post1084105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first part of the Charm makes it sound like it's noticeably less superficial and involves definite shapeshifting. But then, it wouldn't be the first time that a Lunar Charm's text ended up horribly mangled and at odds with itself. Flowing Body Evasion, after all, didn't even tell you if it actually stopped undodgeable or perfect attacks, what the Charm actually looked like, and it went on for like half a page when it was saying nothing.<br /> <br /> And it was Simple type and based on Charisma. The salt floe never ends for FBE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sometimes I wonder whether these Charms are poorly written or if I'm the one that's missing some esoteric insight into Lunar Attributes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">On one hand, I get how you're &quot;manipulating&quot; your body. But on the other, that's not what Manipulation means...</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">... or is it?!</span><br /> <img src=\"https://static.stuff.co.nz/1377728556/480/9101480.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:22:52-07:00","id":1084124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084118#post1084118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sometimes I wonder whether these Charms are poorly written or if I'm the one that's missing some esoteric insight into Lunar Attributes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">On one hand, I get how you're &quot;manipulating&quot; your body. But on the other, that's not what Manipulation means...</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">... or is it?!</span><br /> <img src=\"https://static.stuff.co.nz/1377728556/480/9101480.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. They were terrible. End of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:24:46-07:00","id":1084125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084077#post1084077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case I think it'd be more appropriate to learn to make tools from your hands before making weapons. It feels more like a progression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that breaking things is easier than making things, I disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thing is, the Charm itself is already intrinsically more limited than CNNT in that you're still working as though you had tools, you're not e.g. shaping steel as though it was clay as CNNT, you still need a source of heat and still need to pound it for hours. </div> </div> </div>Good point. I had forgotten any project-speed component of CNNT.<br /> <br /> However, fire-breathing is another thing that a Heart's Blood-oriented version of Tool-Hand Technique could benefit from. If HB Library is measured in Merit dots; even if it isn't, there's stunting potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Taking it down yet another notch just for the sake of it seems entirely unnecessary to me. Just because Lunars have a barbarian aesthetic doesn't mean they're limited to the stone-age in everything they do. </div> </div> </div>That wasn't my point. My point is to start with weak or simple principle effects and build up to complicated or powerful effects.<br /> <br /> &quot;Make my fist a hammer which can break things&quot; is simpler than &quot;use my hammer fist for a variety of careful actions to construct something deliberately&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather I'm just really not fond of WBT, especially now that its only benefit is adding the Lethal tag to what's otherwise the stats of every Light Weapon. </div> </div> </div>Plus allowing you to parry lethal damage bare-handed. But I wasn't specifically referring to an exact copy of the 1st Edition Charm; merely a return of its concept in a form more similar to 2nd Edition's Moonsilver Claws, and then reserving Moonsilver Claws for a more impressive Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:42:21-07:00","id":1084131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084125#post1084125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that breaking things is easier than making things, I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. then we fundamentally disagree *shrug*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Make my fist a hammer which can break things&quot; is simpler than &quot;use my hammer fist for a variety of careful actions to construct something deliberately&quot;. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Melee and Brawl are about much more than just &quot;breaking things&quot;. What you're describing is a Feat of Strength.<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm pretty sure our ideas aren't at all compatible, since they differ on a fundamental game-principles level, so I'm bowing out.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:33:46-07:00","id":1084160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084131#post1084131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is a Feat of Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or an attack.<br /> <br /> But not really that, either. I envision Body Weapon Technique as &quot;make my fist hard&quot;. The Charm doesn't do anything beyond that, and it's up to the Lunar to find a use for his hammer-fist. The simplest use is hitting something. He can also stunt using it as a hammer to drive a nail into a door.<br /> <br /> But a craft project is more involved than that, and involves knowing how to use a hammer constructively, which requires more understanding than the act of swinging a hammer around to hurt and break things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>If you wanted to make BWT and THT the same Charm</b>, that would be different. The Lunar enhances all of his natural features such that they can be more effective weapons or tools. Since the proposed THT doesn't do anything beyond that, there's really no difference.<br /> <br /> It would be a Strength Charm with either name; the other name would be used for a specialized advanced effect or upgrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:49:51-07:00","id":1084166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084118#post1084118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sometimes I wonder whether these Charms are poorly written or if I'm the one that's missing some esoteric insight into Lunar Attributes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">On one hand, I get how you're &quot;manipulating&quot; your body. But on the other, that's not what Manipulation means...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the direct shapeshifting Charms in 1st edition ended up under Manipulation and sometimes Charisma because... I'm not honestly sure. I'd guess it's because there was some kind of idea at the time that &quot;Changing Moons are the unparalleled Shapeshifters of the Lunars&quot; or something along those lines, so most Charms involving shapeshifting fell under Charisma and Manipulation. While 2nd edition Lunars gets a lot of well deserved flack, I think many people forget how incredibly wonky and bizarre 1st edition Lunars were, and what a huge step up 2nd edition was for them in so many respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T16:23:36-07:00","id":1084201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1083978#post1083978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Lunars can feed their blood to others to transform them, I think Lunars can soak their blood into objects made of organic material to reanimate them enough that their healing process assists the Lunar's ability to repair them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a lot of things that are magic are necessarily self-contained.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike how somebody being able to kindle a flame in their hand or cause something to combust doesn't mean anything about them being able to manipulate energy in a general sense.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the Lunar narrative and essense that drives their magic could do a lot of things with living things that it wouldn't with inanimate objects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T19:00:21-07:00","id":1084243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1084166#post1084166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of the direct shapeshifting Charms in 1st edition ended up under Manipulation and sometimes Charisma because... I'm not honestly sure. I'd guess it's because there was some kind of idea at the time that &quot;Changing Moons are the unparalleled Shapeshifters of the Lunars&quot; or something along those lines, so most Charms involving shapeshifting fell under Charisma and Manipulation. While 2nd edition Lunars gets a lot of well deserved flack, I think many people forget how incredibly wonky and bizarre 1st edition Lunars were, and what a huge step up 2nd edition was for them in so many respects.</div> </div> </div> </div>A shame about that core concept being scattered to the far corners of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:31:21-07:00","id":1086249,"title":"","content":"Remind me; Ability-based Exalted (or at least Solars) cannot use a Craft Charm for a Craft in which they don't have enough dots to meet the Charm's minimums?<br /> <br /> But the Lunar Charm &quot;Tool-Hand Technique&quot; would be Ability-agnostic because it is an Attribute Charm. No matter how high the Charm's Attribute minimum, it can be applied to any Craft project the Lunar attempts even if they only have a single dot in that Craft. Meanwhile, a Solar can only use &quot;Craftsman Needs No Tools&quot; if he has at least THREE dots in the Craft he wants to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tool-Hand Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m; <b>Mins: </b>Intelligence 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One task<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Without the need for tools or a workshop, the Exalt can start basic crafting projects as soon as she has the proper ingredients. If the Lunar player stunts how her character uses her own features and secretions --- claws, silk, poison, or fire-breath, as examples -- as tools, she reduces the cost of the Charm by the number of stunt dice the Storyteller grants her.<br /> <br /> <br /> This proposed Charm is automatically broader in scope than Craftsman Needs No Tools, since it can apply to ANY crafting project, so long as the Lunar has at least ONE dot in the associated Craft. Therefore, it CANNOT be allowed to be as good as the Solar equivalent.<br /> <br /> So, I feel comfortable in excluding any speed-boosting effect, and requiring synergy with the follow Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Body-Weapon Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Exalt infuses her body with Essence, allowing her to bring fists to a knife-fight. For the rest of the scene, the Lunar may parry lethal and ranged weapons bare-handed, and may inflict lethal damage with natural weapons that normally only inflict bashing.<br /> <br /> A Lunar who knows this Charm can now use Tool-Hand Technique to work on major projects without tools.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-01-2017, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:53:24-07:00","id":1086257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1086249#post1086249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me; Ability-based Exalted (or at least Solars) cannot use a Craft Charm for a Craft in which they don't have enough dots to meet the Charm's minimums?<br /> <br /> But the Lunar Charm &quot;Tool-Hand Technique&quot; would be Ability-agnostic because it is an Attribute Charm. No matter how high the Charm's Attribute minimum, it can be applied to any Craft project the Lunar attempts even if they only have a single dot in that Craft. Meanwhile, a Solar can only use &quot;Craftsman Needs No Tools&quot; if he has at least THREE dots in the Craft he wants to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1075202#post1075202\">Not quite.</a> Once you've bought the Charm, you can use it with any Craft ability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T11:05:53-07:00","id":1086261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bozwevial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1086257#post1086257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1075202#post1075202\">Not quite.</a> Once you've bought the Charm, you can use it with any Craft ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks.<br /> <br /> Must have been an idea discarded for the final draft of the Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T10:46:26-07:00","id":1087226,"title":"","content":"It sounds good, as long as Lunars do get a way to do something fast, like from a repurchase of the base charm. I would expect weaknesses of lunar crafting charms (compared to solar ones, at least) would be when it came to really massive projects or maybe in drawbacks for some of their tricks, such as the created object or the repair being only temporary or requiring extra maintenance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:54:18-07:00","id":1087262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1079494-lunars-and-interacting-with-the-base-crafting-system?p=1087226#post1087226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds good, as long as Lunars do get a way to do something fast, like from a repurchase of the base charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like a general &quot;work faster&quot; Charm, like the Alchemicals got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T13:34:21-07:00","id":1087321,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;problem&quot; Lunar crafters are going to run into is that craft rolls aren't necessarily tied to a specific attribute. So you might wind up with a situation where a lunar crafter needs to buy into both the Stamina tree for a charm that lets them work longer hours and the Intelligence tree for a charm that lets them get more crafting points. Then they might need to go into the Wits tree for some other effect and the Dexterity tree for another effect.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, I don't think that's a bad thing. Lunars aren't Solars so I fully expect the structure of their charm trees to encourage diversification to one extent or another. Hopefully this won't be done in a way that makes playing a Lunar crafter not fun (which it could easily turn into if a PC has to buy into any one tree too much before they can get to the effects they want). But I would be surprised if crafting charms were as centralized for attribute based exalted as they are for ability based exalted.<br /> <br /> Other than that one obstacle, I think Lunar's are only going to have trouble generating the most powerful of artifacts and manses. In most ways they'll be able to rival the Solars if not equal them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:20:20-07:00","id":1087438,"title":"","content":"Which is thematically appropriate for Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}